Based on your feedback, I've identified the root cause. The "Symmetry ignored" issue and the "First segment" behavior are related to how the system handles **Reverse Direction Matching**.

When the system checks a segment in reverse (e.g., traversing a line right-to-left instead of left-to-right), it effectively flips the coordinate system by 180 degrees. Mathematically, this causes **relative angles to flip sign** (a Left turn becomes a Right turn). Previously, this "double flip" allowed the system to accidentally match **Mirrored Geometry** via the "Reverse" logic, even if symmetry was disabled. Additionally, matching in reverse places punches relative to the *end* of the segment, which can visually appear as if the "first segment punches are wrong/missing" if the match wasn't intended.

I will update `services/teachLogic.ts` to strictly enforce geometry winding rules. If we check in reverse, we must now expect the *opposite* turns and arc curvatures to match the *original* shape, preventing accidental mirror matching.

